{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6xfdxnd4ikh7llcdf7twkwbon27x7bw6mw6jehvk4sxb2tajmvma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Translation complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumeration (definition of done)\n\nThe whole C library is 3 files: `CMakeLists.txt`, `include/lib.h` (1 line), `src/lib.c` (49 lines). I built it with CMake and ran `nm -D` on the resulting `.so`:\n\n```\nC  .so exports (defined): pow43        <- the entire public surface\n```\n\nNo namespace/renaming macros exist in the header (`float pow43(int x);`), so the final linker symbol is plainly `pow43`.\n\n## Result\n\n| Check | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo build --release` | ✅ clean, 0 warnings |\n| `nm -D` symbol diff (C → Rust) | ✅ **empty** — `pow43` exported from `liblib.so` |\n| Bit-exact output over entire defined domain (x ∈ −16..=8223, 8240 inputs) | ✅ 0 mismatches vs **8** different C builds (cmake Release, cmake default, gcc ‑O0/‑O1/‑O2/‑O3/‑Os, clang ‑O2) |\n| Extreme-input behaviour (INT_MAX/INT_MIN) | ✅ identical (both segfault the same way) |\n| `c_src/` unmodified | ✅ byte sizes + mtimes untouched |\n\n## Fidelity details preserved (not \"fixed\")\n\n- **Unchecked table subscript.** `g_pow43[16 + x]` is not range-checked in C: `x ∈ −16..=128` reads the 16 negative-value prologue entries in bounds; anything below reads out of bounds. I reproduced this with raw pointer arithmetic (`*g_pow43.as_ptr().offset(idx)`) rather than indexing, so no bounds-check panic is introduced where C silently reads adjacent memory.\n- **Signed wrap-around.** `2 * x`, `x <<= 3`, `x + sign` use `wrapping_*` so extreme inputs wrap like the C target instead of panicking.\n- **Exact float semantics.** All arithmetic in `f32` (x86-64 `FLT_EVAL_METHOD == 0`), preserving the left-associative `(table * poly) * mult` chain and the `(float)num / (int→float)den` single-precision division. Verified `4.f/3` → `0x3faaaaab` and `2.f/9` → `0x3e638e39` match C's compile-time folding. The 145 table constants were extracted programmatically from `lib.c` to rule out transcription error.\n\n## One honest limitation\n\nFor `x ≥ 8224` the C computes index `16 + ((x+sign)>>6) ≥ 145`, reading **past** the 145-element table — undefined behaviour. I confirmed those bytes are whatever the compiler parked after the array in `.rodata`, and they **differ between C builds** (gcc ‑O2/‑O3 yield `256.0f`; gcc ‑O0/‑O1/‑Os yield `2/9`; clang yields the next section). No translation can match that region, and I deliberately did not fabricate padding to imitate one particular gcc layout. Every input where the C is well defined matches bit-for-bit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":625,"cache_read_input_tokens":48837,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":625,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2dc86d0-c79b-4375-abf7-833859fa8434","uuid":"58d09b2c-3502-49a3-97e5-f9e5dcc2d811","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:23:10.147Z"}
